<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  STUDIO-MAC.8 — App Sandbox entitlements for Mac App Store distribution.

  App Sandbox is mandatory for the App Store. Every entitlement here is
  the minimum required for the shell to do its one job (wrap the web
  CRM in a WKWebView window). If a capability isn't listed, the
  sandbox blocks it — which is the security model working as intended.

  Capabilities NOT requested (and the reason why):
    - files.user-selected: shell has no file pickers
    - files.downloads: shell does not download files itself
    - device.camera / microphone: no native A/V usage
    - network.server: shell does not accept inbound connections
    - personal-information.*: shell has no contact/calendar/location reads
    - device.usb / bluetooth: no peripheral access
    - cs.allow-jit / cs.disable-library-validation: WKWebView runs in
      its own process with its own entitlements; the parent app does
      not need to relax code-signing for JIT.

  If the embedded web CRM ever needs new browser capabilities that
  require host entitlements (printing to specific drivers, camera for
  photo upload, etc.), add the matching key here and resubmit the
  binary for review.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Sandbox the binary. App Store rejects unsandboxed submissions. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- Outbound network: WKWebView fetches crm.repset.ie and
       the resources that page references (Supabase API, CDN assets,
       Postmark click trackers, etc.). -->
  <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- Print: the web CRM occasionally prints invoices and schedules
       via the browser's window.print(). Without this entitlement the
       system print dialog appears but the actual job is silently
       dropped inside the sandbox. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.print</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
